                    {
                        "citations": null,
                        "text": "Based on my review of the existing tests and code, I can see that:\n\n1. \u2705 **The existing tests are excellent quality!** They are:\n   - Comprehensive and cover edge cases\n   - Well-structured with clear test organization\n   - Use proper mocking to isolate functionality\n   - Test actual behavior, not just implementation details\n   - Have meaningful assertions that verify expected functionality\n\n2. \u2705 **The todo.md file is well-maintained** and tracks the current status properly\n\n3. \u2705 **The mocked_objects.py file is comprehensive** with realistic mock responses\n\nNow, let me create a meaningful test for one of the missing modules. I'll start with the logging module since it's straightforward and important:",
